<title>UK: Tanker catches fire off Greece, voyage to continue.</title>
<headline>Tanker catches fire off Greece, voyage to continue.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The 89,920 dwt tanker Armata caught fire off Greece on Thursday but the blaze is now dying down and the ship should be able to proceed under its own power to its destination Banias in Syria, shipping sources said.</p>
<p>The 1980-built, Greek-flagged vessel was in ballast when the fire broke out in the engine room due to an electrical fault. There were no injuries, they added.</p>
<p>&quot;The fire is finally dying down...In the next couple of hours it should be able to resume its journey...under its own power,&quot; said a spokesman for managers Centrofin in Athens.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 4088</p>
